  "notes": "Generated from a published construction, not transcribed and not new. TT(36) = (X, Y, Z, W) is the hexadecimal string that SageMath stores for n = 36 and credits to Kharaghani and Tayfeh-Rezaie. A = Z;W, B = Z;-W, C = X, D = Y are base sequences of lengths 71, 71, 36, 36, and T_1 = (A+B)/2;0, T_2 = (A-B)/2;0, T_3 = 0;(C+D)/2, T_4 = 0;(C-D)/2 are T-sequences of length 107. The rows are T_1+T_2+T_3+T_4, -T_1+T_2+T_3-T_4, -T_1-T_2+T_3+T_4 and -T_1+T_2-T_3+T_4, whose Goethals-Seidel array is the Cooper-Wallis Hadamard matrix of order 428. The script in the evidence file checks the Turyn-type identity, the base-sequence identity, the T-sequence support and identity, and the PAF identity of the rows. Not checked: whether this matrix is equivalent to the one printed in the 2005 paper. The board had no quadruple at n = 107 before."
